.SS "\fBHash64\fP SystemEx\&.Hash\&.BernsteinHash\&.ComputeLong (FixedVector< byte > input, ulong seed)"

.PP
Computes a simple 64‑bit hash from the given byte sequence\&. The hash starts with the provided \fIseed\fP  and mixes each byte using a larger multiplier (1315423911), a common constant used in JSHash‑style Bernstein derivatives to improve diffusion in 64‑bit space\&.

.PP
\fBEndian\fP does not affect this algorithm directly; it is included for interface compatibility with other \fBSystemEx\fP hashers\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP The input data to hash\&.
.br
\fIseed\fP The seed value for the hash computation\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The computed Bernstein hash as a \fBHash64\fP object\&.
.RE
